{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3423","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3423","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3423\",\"parent_revision\":\"6f7013107acf9b48551967608819ff0dd6fcf2e10ce1bba797b6075eddfe892f\",\"root_revision\":\"6f7013107acf9b48551967608819ff0dd6fcf2e10ce1bba797b6075eddfe892f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-06\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe sub-agent completion contract pins the first line of a worker's final message to `STATUS: DONE | PARTIAL | BLOCKED`. Several dh agents load `dh:subagent-contract` but emit their own domain verdict on that line instead, so a dispatcher branching on the contract tokens matches nothing and cannot tell whether the step succeeded.\\n\\nImpact if this stands: the orchestrator's \\\"did this step succeed?\\\" decision reads a token it does not recognise. It cannot distinguish a completed step from a blocked one for these agents, so it either proceeds past a failed step or stalls on a successful one. Same failure class as the SubagentStop laundering defect fixed in this session, one layer up.\\n\\nExit criterion: `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_status_token_vocabulary_drift.py::test_every_status_token_is_registered` passes. That test exists and currently fails; its failure output is the worklist.\\n\\nWorklist as of 2026-09-06 \u2014 5 unregistered tokens across 3 agents:\\n- `STATUS: VERIFIED`, `STATUS: GAPS_FOUND` \u2014 agents/feature-verifier.md\\n- `STATUS: GAPS_FOUND`, `STATUS: CONNECTED` \u2014 agents/integration-checker.md\\n- `STATUS: READY`, `STATUS: DRAFTING` \u2014 agents/plan-validator.md\\n\\nOpen question for grooming: whether these agents report a contract token on the STATUS line and carry their domain verdict on a separate labelled line, or whether the contract admits registered per-agent verdict schemas.\\n\\nAlso in scope: `STATUS: COMPLETE` still has producers in agents/task-worker.md and skills/work-milestone/, and the SubagentStop hook accepts it. So the divergence runs in both directions \u2014 agents emit tokens the contract does not name, and the hook accepts tokens the contract does not name.\\n\\nSequencing: downstream of agent-orchestration PR #3422, which pins the three-token contract repo-wide.\\n\\nRelated: #2182 covers worker preflight self-check and worker-report structure. This item is narrower \u2014 the token vocabulary itself and its drift guard \u2014 and does not supersede it.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: the permissive `DONE|COMPLETE|COMPLETED` matcher in the SubagentStop hook is deliberate temporary breadth carrying a `ponytail:` marker, and stays until this item narrows it. `COMPLETED` was verified to have zero producers anywhere in plugins/ and is accepted defensively only.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: DH delegation-spine audit, session melodic-plotting-emerson (2026-09-06)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"b0b16250a25605147a196cae20fc7eb536b84f06cc574b794fbf31c5b09f17e1\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABTSBJ2A\"}"}